# Testing Rules

The definition of "working" is `docs/TEST_PLAN.md` — its checklists are the acceptance criteria for every task.

## Server tests (Vitest + supertest — `server/tests/`)

- `unit/` — pure functions only (matcher, keyword extraction, CSV escaping). No DB, no mocks needed for these.
- `integration/` — real HTTP against the app + test database: happy path, auth failure (401), role failure (403), validation failure (400), conflict (409).
- Fixtures for the matcher must include the exact cases from TEST_PLAN §4 (100 / 0 / 50.0 / determinism).

## Client E2E (Playwright — `client/e2e/`)

- Scenarios come from TEST_PLAN §10 (E2E-1 … E2E-6). Each test starts from a clean state.
- Full user flows only — do not re-test what unit tests cover.

## Workflow

- After implementing: lint → typecheck → run the tests for the touched area. Fix failures before reporting done.
- Never delete or skip a failing test to "make it pass" — report it instead.
- When adding a feature, add its checks to TEST_PLAN.md if missing, then implement to that standard.
